{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774714,"nonce":"qBYo3DtOYGd8h8ZJAx0PA7h/S+g=","title":"fix: provision the clone-token Secret in-cluster (RBAC grant + create-409 launch race)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #24 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/step-clone-secret-provisioning` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-17T18:51:12Z · Merged: 2026-07-17T18:53:25Z\n\n\nOn a hardened in-cluster Helm deploy, a step's checkout Pod could hang in `FailedMount` forever — `secret \"\u003cpod\u003e-token\" not found` — and the run would hot-loop or dead-letter instead of cloning. Two independent gaps, both in the clone-token Secret lifecycle (ADR-0045; same shape applies to the OIDC token ADR-0015 and registry dockerconfig ADR-0018):\n\n1. **Missing RBAC.** The executor `Role` granted `pods`, `pods/log`, `pods/status`, `pods/exec` — but **not `secrets`**. The k8s executor upserts a per-Pod Secret before a step runs (`ensure_clone_secret` / `ensure_oidc_secret` / `ensure_registry_secret`), so `secrets.create()` returned **403**; the Secret the Pod mounts was never created.\n\n2. **create-409 launch race.** `K8sExecutor::launch` upserts those Secrets on the fresh-create and re-attach paths, but the **create-409 branch** (a concurrent launcher or a re-drive won the create race) returned `Ok` *without* provisioning them. If the create winner made the Pod but hadn't (or never) provisioned the Secrets, the 409-loser reported success, the scheduler moved to `poll()`, and nothing ever (re)created the Secret.\n\n\n- **`deploy/helm/scarab/templates/rbac.yaml`** — grant the executor `Role` `resources: [secrets]`, `verbs: [get, create, update]`. Each Secret is owner-referenced to its Pod (GC'd on Pod delete, so no `delete` verb); `update` backs the short-TTL re-drive refresh (replace-in-place on 409).\n- **`crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs`** — on create-409, fetch the live Pod and run the same secret upserts (owner-referenced to it), mirroring the re-attach path. The three `ensure_*_secret` calls, now needed in three places, are folded into one idempotent `ensure_step_secrets` helper so the paths can't drift again — that drift is what left the 409 branch behind.\n\n\nDriven end-to-end in-cluster (colima) on the real multi-arch GHA image `ghcr.io/thulasi-ram/scarab-server:sha-ee58641…`:\n\n- **Public repo** (`scarab-ci`): real GitHub push webhook → run → clone via a minted `contents:read` token (no 422, no anonymous fallback) → `cargo check` → `pending`→`success` commit status with a resolvable deep-link.\n- **Private repo** (`agent_foundry`): clone succeeds **only** via the minted token (anonymous can't clone a private repo); `.git/config` is credential-free (S2 — the token rides GIT_ASKPASS/tmpfs); status posts back on the private repo.\n\n`cargo test -p scarab-executor-k8s`: 28 passed, 12 ignored (live-cluster).\n\nThe 409 race is control flow around the k8s API (no fake-client harness in this crate), so it isn't unit-tested; the fresh-create path that shares `ensure_step_secrets` is exercised by the green runs above.\n\ngit-bug: `b06b048` (RBAC), `1b5d5c7` (clone contents:read, verified alongside).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}